### Tree-Cover Change Summary

Between 2020 and 2024, the analysis identified approximately **13.78 km² (1,378.42 ha)** of candidate tree-cover loss within Juaboso District.

The change layer was derived from pixels classified as **Trees in 2020** and **non-Trees in 2024**. Small isolated changes were removed using a connected-pixel threshold of 100 pixels (~1 ha).

These results represent land-cover-classification-based tree-cover change and should not be interpreted directly as confirmed deforestation without further validation.
